I have recently become aware of my use of {do} for the "general you" and I 
don't think that's good; it's a common source of confusion in English. {doi 
ma}? Perhaps {lo'e prenu} (lo su'a prenu?) is better, but I wonder if 
something in KOhA7 might be useful? (maybe one of Curtis' infamous zmico 
already means that; but I can't understand their descriptions)

By the way in English, I think I'll try to use the word "one" instead of 
the general-you; it's a lost art. I can't tell you* how many times I've 
accidentally insulted people with the "general you".

*can't tell one? Well this also happens to apply to anyone who reads this...

